id: pm-gh1775
title: "GH-1775: the secret guard flags bare environment-variable references (api_key: ${API_KEY}) as credentials since the #1704 widening"
description: "GH-1775 (filed 2026-11-23 while moving the extension package pm-memory to 2026.11.23; draft unbraind/pm-memory#96 is blocked on it). Since the credential-key guard widened beyond password (pm-gh1704), scanMutationSecrets reports credential_key_assignment for a value made only of a reference under a credential key: scanMutationSecrets(JSON.stringify({ title: 'api_key: ${API_KEY}', updated: '2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z' })) returns [] on 2026.11.14 and a credential_key_assignment finding on 2026.11.23. A reference names where a secret lives and holds no secret value, so trackers that document configuration (api_key: ${API_KEY}, token=$GITHUB_TOKEN) have their mutations refused. pm-hw00c2 (closed) made CREDENTIAL_VALUE capture a value that holds a run-time reference whole and judge the literal left after expansion; a bare reference leaves no literal, so whether it should still match is the question this item settles. Expected: a value made only of a reference (${NAME}, $NAME, ${{ secrets.NAME }} and similar) is not a credential under any credential key; a reference with an attached literal or a literal value is still flagged. Duplicate check: searched secret guard environment variable reference credential key bare reference; pm-hw00c2, pm-ycgb5g and pm-gh1704 are closed and own the literal-concatenation and key-widening rules."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"gh:1775",regression,secret-guard,security
